# Repo-wide safety net: this repo tracks SOURCE ONLY (scripts, SKILL.md, README,
# reference docs). Nothing pulled from Jira, generated by a run, or containing
# credentials may ever be committed — from any directory, under any name.
#
# These rules are deliberately broad and match by extension, not by filename, so
# a new artifact with an unforeseen name is ignored by default rather than
# committed by accident. scripts/.gitignore adds the by-name patterns on top.
#
# Adding a legitimate non-data file that one of these patterns catches?
# Un-ignore it explicitly (a `!pattern` line here), don't `git add -f` it —
# an -f add is invisible to the next person.

# --- credentials ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# --- pulled Jira data, analysis output, plans, run ledgers ---
# Every JSON in this repo is data. The only exceptions are re-included below.
*.json
!.claude/*.json
!**/*.example.json
*.jsonl
*.csv
*.tsv

# --- generated deliverables ---
*.xlsx
*.docx
*.pdf
*.pptx
Bug_*.md
NEEDS_REVIEW_*.md
report_*.md

# --- logs & intermediates ---
logs/
*.log
_*.txt

# --- local junk ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Python
.venv/
venv/
